            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Well, it turns out the problem as I originally reported is back...\n\nI had a workaround in `.tmux.conf` (a hook that would send `C-z` then `fg` after a tmux pane resizes). Before testing, I deactivated the hook and started a new tmux session. After posting my last message, I decided to tweak the hook and accidentally messed something up, so I deactivated it again and started another new tmux session. Now nvim doesn't resize correctly when resizing tmux up/down or left/right, as I originally reported. Perhaps I didn't close all tmux sessions when I tested...\n\n> > `kill -WINCH <nvim_pid>` (sent from another pane) has no effect.\n> \n> This still seems weird. However, it depends on multiple things, e.g. `$LINES/$COLUMNS` env vars in your shell may have been set. \n> \n> There is also an interaction with `resize_events_enabled` , I don't remember the details though, but it could be terminal (tmux) related. \n\nConfirmed that `kill -WINCH <nvim_pid>` still has no effect with v0.12.4 and the latest nightly. I'll take a look at tui.c when I have the chance and see if I can find any other clues as to what's happening.",
